          "subComponents": [
            {
              "description": {
                "type": "textComponent",
                "text": "As part of the 2014 Imperial College London iGEM team I helped develop customisable bacterial cellulose-based ultrafiltration membranes using synthetic biology approaches. \n\nAs part of the diverse team I saw the project through from initial brainstorming to prototyping. Through our efforts we achieved 2nd place in the world at the international jamboree in Boston as well as winning the Manufacturing Track and several other awards. \n\nIn addition to the group tasks my primary responsibility was the development of the website to host information about the project as well as the design and construction of the conference poster. This involved coordinating between the various sub-teams to create a consistent yet technical narrative."
